### 0. Definitions

- **"Software"** means the source code, object code, documentation
  (including README.md and this LICENSE file), and any associated
  assets (including logos, icons, trademarks, user interface layout,
  visual design, and interaction patterns) contained in this
  repository, in any version. **"Software" also includes any
  compiled, packaged, minified, or obfuscated build of the foregoing
  (including but not limited to `.crx`, `.xpi`, and other browser
  extension installation packages), and any code obtained by
  decompiling, deobfuscating, or otherwise reverse-engineering such a
  build, regardless of whether it was obtained from this repository
  or from a published, distributed copy.**
- **"Derivative Work"** means any work that modifies, translates,
  adapts, or is based on the Software, in whole or in substantial
  part, regardless of the percentage of lines changed, including but
  not limited to: rebranded forks, ports to other platforms, works
  that incorporate substantial portions of the Software's source
  code, logic, or architecture, and works generated by removing,
  adding to, or reorganizing the Software's files.
- **"Public Distribution"** means making the Software or a Derivative
  Work available to any third party, by any means, including but not
  limited to: publishing to a code hosting platform in a manner
  accessible to the public, publishing to an app store, browser
  extension store, or software marketplace, hosting as a public web
  service, or bundling with another distributed product.
- **"Personal, Non-Commercial Use"** means use by a single natural
  person, for that person's own private purposes, where no revenue,
  business advantage, or benefit to any organization (including the
  user's employer) is derived from such use, and where the Software
  is not made available to any other person. Use within, for the
  benefit of, or on behalf of a business, non-profit, government
  entity, or any other organization is not Personal, Non-Commercial
  Use, regardless of whether payment is involved.
- **"Competing Product or Service"** means any product or service
  that provides functionality substantially similar to the Software's
  core functionality (browser-based translation of web content) to
  any third party or the public, regardless of pricing model, branding,
  or the degree of code modification involved.
- **"Attribution"** means the unmodified copyright notice and the
  full, unmodified text of this License, prominently included in any
  permitted copy or Derivative Work. A brief mention of the
  Software's name elsewhere in documentation (e.g., a single line
  stating "modified from [Software]") does not, by itself, satisfy
  this requirement.
- **"Presumption of Derivation"**: if a work exhibits substantial
  similarity to the Software in architecture, code organization,
  naming conventions, comment style, or other non-functional
  characteristics, that work is presumed to be a Derivative Work of
  the Software absent clear evidence to the contrary (such as an
  independent, complete version-control history predating any access
  to the Software).

